 type of interlocutor."}, {"type": "secondary_4", "content": "Identifies general information in short written or spoken conversations."}, {"type": "secondary_5", "content": "Identifies general information in short written or spoken conversations."}, {"type": "secondary_6", "content": "Gives appropriate directions to places taking into account the type of interlocutor."}, {"type": "secondary_7", "content": "Gives appropriate directions to places taking into account the type of interlocutor."}, {"type": "secondary_8", "content": "Gives appropriate directions to places taking into account the type of interlocutor."}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": " Using Wh-Questions"}, {"type": "describer", "content": " "}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"strong\">When and Where</span><br><br>You use when to ask questions about time.<br> You use where to ask questions about location.<br>  <br>In the present, the form is<br>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "  <center>when/where + am/is/are/do/does + person/thing + verb ?</center>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Examples:<span class=\"italic\"><br>When do we arrive at the butterfly farm?<br> Where does he live?<br></span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"strong\">Which</span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "You use <span class=\"strong\">which </span> to ask questions about a person or thing in a group."}, {"type": "text", "content": "In the present, the form is"}, {"type": "text", "content": " <center>which + noun + am/is/are/do/does + rest of sentence or person/thing + verb ?</center>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Example:<br><span class=\"italic\">Which bus is in front of the restaurant?</span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"strong\">How</span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "You use <span class=\"strong\">how</span> to ask \u201cin what way\u201d"}, {"type": "text", "content": "In the present, the form is"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<center>how or how + expressions + am/is/are/do/does + rest of sentence or person/thing + verb ?</center>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Example:<br><span class=\"italic\">How much does it cost?</span>"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "cage "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a box made of wire or metal bars in which people keep animals or birds "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Butterflies are not kept in cages!"}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn4le03ob04aud01"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "These are words you hear on a guided tour."}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "enclosure "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "an area surrounded by a wall, fence or netting"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: The butterfly farm has many enclosures."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn4le03ob04aud02"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "species"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a group of animals or plants that are similar"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: There are many different species of animals at the zoo."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn4le03ob04aud03"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "rainforest "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a tropical forest that receives a lot of rain and has very tall trees"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: It always rains in the Costa Rican rainforest!"}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn4le03ob04aud04"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "cloud"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a white or gray mass in the sky that is made of many very small drops of water"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: There are many clouds in the sky today."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn4le03ob04aud05"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "downpour "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a sudden, heavy rain  "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I hope there isn't a downpour. I forgot my umbrella."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn4le03ob04aud06"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "plantation"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a large area of land where you grow crops"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: We visited a coffee plantation."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn4le03ob04aud07"}]}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "engenn4le03ob04re1img01.png"}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Research a coffee plantation tour in your area or in another country."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Write five Wh-questions you would ask. Example: <span class=\"italic\">How much is the entry fee?</span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Practice your questions aloud using falling intonation."}, {"type": "text", "content": " Share your questions with a partner."}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I identify guided tours."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I ask various questions to get information."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I write complete questions that ask for information."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I practice asking questions using falling intonation."}]}], "type": "sena"}